Content area from OpenRune/OpenRune-Server#353 (answers there: all of it, one PR per row, ids renumbered against main, wiki data is fine).

From our per-feature patches `48-grand-exchange`, `50-ge-partial-fills-and-buy-limits`, `51-ge-trade-history`, `52-ge-tax-exempt-items` (in [`openrune/upstream/`](https://github.com/AlexPerrin/osrs-plugins-reverse/tree/main/openrune/upstream) of osrs-plugins-reverse), on `main` (`c2492318d`).

**Problem.** OpenRune had no Grand Exchange.

**Change.** New modules `content/interfaces/grand-exchange` + pack, in four commits, one per patch, each on the one before:
- **Core (48):** the clerks' Exchange opens `ge_offers` (465) + `ge_offers_side` (467); buy (item search) and sell offers with the setup buttons, Confirm, Abort, Collect / Collect-all, and the banker's Collection Box (402); slot state in UPDATE_STOCKMARKET_SLOT, items in the cache's per-slot invs (enum 150). The server is the only counterparty: offers at or better than the guide price (store cost) fill at the guide, others stay open until aborted; 2% tax.
- **Partial fills and buy limits (50):** fills in up to four parts (2 ticks after Confirm, then every 5 ticks) with partial slot updates and "Grand Exchange: Bought/Sold n / total" lines; buys count against the item's 4-hour limit (enum `ge_buy_limits`).
- **History (51):** the clerks' History op and the History button open `ge_history` (383), filled by scripts 1644-1646 with the last 40 trades, newest first, with the sale tax; Buy-offer on a line starts a buy offer.
- **Tax exemptions (52):** enum `ge_tax_exempt` (bonds, low-level ammo and food, teleport tablets, basic tools...).

Server-only ids, numbered after the ids already on main and not shared with any of our other PRs, so they merge in any order: varps 63796-63955 (history, 4 per line), 63956-64004 (offers), 64005-64052 (buy limits); enums `ge_buy_limits` 64441, `ge_tax_exempt` 64442; timer `ge_offer_fill` 437.

**Tests.** `GrandExchangeScriptTest` (integration).

On this branch (Docker `eclipse-temurin:21`, upstream's `./gradlew`, 4 GB container; a clean `freshCache` of main restored first, then `:or-cache:buildCache :or-cache:mergePluginGamevals`, then each task as a separate run, then `run` to "Server ready"): RESULTS_PENDING. `tools/scripts/fix_gameval_conflicts.py --check` finds no conflicts on this branch, nor with all of our open content PRs merged together.

Nothing was checked in game from this exact branch; the in-game checks above were on our own server build (an older main plus these and our other patches).

**Data sources.** Interfaces, scripts and invs from the cache. OSRS Wiki (by the wiki's contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/): `ge_buy_limits.toml` is generated from the wiki's `Module:GELimits/data.json` (4,186 items) and `ge_tax_exempt.toml` from the Grand Exchange page's "Exempt from tax" section; both files say so in their headers.

**Caveats.**
- **Needs two fixes outside this PR to work in game:** the long-varp compiler issue (#352: long varps compile to the int varp opcodes, so an empty slot shows an offer) and the RSProt bump to `1.0.0-ALPHA-20261014` (UPDATE_STOCKMARKET_SLOT reset wrote slot 0). Neither is in this branch; the integration tests don't hit them.
- No sets, custom % buttons, platinum tokens or connected limits (e.g. potion doses); the partial-fill wording is a guess; unlisted tradeables have no limit.
- History is recorded when the offer finishes or is aborted (OSRS's exact moment is unverified).

**Release note.** A Grand Exchange against the server: buy/sell offers, partial fills, buy limits, collection, history, tax exemptions.

